From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] signal: report no hardware breakpoints in an exception's
 context

save_context filled a context's registers but not its debug registers
(Bcr, Bvr, Wcr, Wvr), so the context an exception handler got held the
stack's leftovers there. Windows reports the hardware breakpoints and
watchpoints that are set: none. World of Warcraft's ARM64 client reads
them in its vectored handler, took the leftovers for a debugger's and
continued at a decoy (pc +0x53e8 with x1 = 0), where the game failed
with "Game Initialization Failed". They are zero now.

Linear: PLA-514
Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-31-wow-arm64-start.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 2185874..e54da25 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -6464,6 +6464,13 @@ static void save_context( CONTEXT *context, const ucontext_t *sigcontext )
     for (i = 0; i <= 28; i++) context->X[i] = REGn_sig( i, sigcontext );
     if (save_fpu( context->V, &context->Fpcr, &context->Fpsr, sigcontext ))
         context->ContextFlags |= CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT;
+    /* Playport (PLA-514): no hardware breakpoint or watchpoint is set, as
+     * Windows reports them; the fields were the stack's leftovers, which
+     * World of Warcraft's vectored handler took for a debugger's. */
+    memset( context->Bcr, 0, sizeof(context->Bcr) );
+    memset( context->Bvr, 0, sizeof(context->Bvr) );
+    memset( context->Wcr, 0, sizeof(context->Wcr) );
+    memset( context->Wvr, 0, sizeof(context->Wvr) );
 }
 
 
